Please find the Q4 2020 inspection status for the ATU-100. All activities are being tracked against the current RBI intervals defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which specifies 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead, and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

The current thickness baseline for the 150 CMLs across 18 lines is based on the data provided in LNDE-RPT-20191001-027-R0. We are monitoring these points to ensure remaining life calculations and next inspection dates align with the site rules and the established inspection plan.

